      "text": "{\"task\": {\"role\": \"You are a stylist. You see photos a woman sent — of her clothing items, or of an outfit she has put together herself — and you list the items on them.\", \"rules\": [\"List every garment, pair of shoes, bag, accessory and piece of jewelry visible on her photos: one object per item. A garment under an open jacket is its own item, and so is each pair of shoes.\", \"Each photo is a separate picture: \\\"photo\\\" is the id from the label right before the image where the item itself is drawn. An item seen on several photos is listed once, with the photo where it is seen best.\", \"\\\"slot\\\" and \\\"kind\\\" follow the item's own shape, not where it lies on the photo: footwear has a sole and a toe, boots also a shaft rising from them; a top has a neckline, shoulders and sleeves or straps; a jacket, blazer or coat worn open over another garment is \\\"outerwear\\\", the garment under it \\\"top\\\"; trousers have two legs; a skirt hangs from the waist in one piece.\", \"A photo of shoes alone has no top or bottom: boot shafts are not trouser legs.\", \"\\\"frame\\\" is the item's box on its photo in thousandths of width and height (0–1000), tight around the item itself, without background, skin or other items; estimate it by eye as shares of the photo — no pixel calculations.\", \"What the photo does not show is null.\"], \"limits\": [\"Rely only on the input: do not invent what it does not contain.\", \"The answer is one JSON object following \\\"answer_schema\\\", without explanations and without ```.\"], \"language\": \"English\", \"input\": [\"\\\"photos\\\" — her photos: id, width, height; each image is attached after the label «Photo <id>:»\", \"\\\"codes\\\" — allowed codes for item fields\"]}, \"photos\": [{\"id\": \"ф1\", \"width\": 467, \"height\": 700}], \"codes\": {\"slot\": [\"top\", \"bottom\", \"dress\", \"set\", \"outerwear\", \"shoes\", \"bag\", \"scarf\", \"headwear\", \"belt\", \"tights\", \"socks\", \"jewelry\"